Hello all,

first I would like say that there's no YAFAP from me.Never brought
myself to write it and everything is forgotten now. My apologies if
that is considered unpolite.

First five ascensions (V,W,K,Rog,S) happened in spring this year.
All seemed to come out easlily after I had first reached the
catle. 
Always curious about the tourist-class, I started to play them and
liked the challenge in the early-game. (previously I disliked that)

Anyway, after the unfortunate deaths of Zing 1,Zing 2 and Zing 3,
I got lucky on my fourth attemt with Fructal the (this time randomly 
generated) female human neutral Tourist ! Just unbelievable for me.

Fructal, BTW is the name of my favourite orange-syrup, but this is
going off-topic.

[I have to say that I don't remember the exact sequence in whitch 
 things happened, the following is mostly from my notes .]

Here are my starting stats

St:18/01  Dx:10  Co:13  In:13  Wi:9  Ch:13

Good strength, all right.
Second room ,lost my pet to a falling-rock trap. Dammit.
Previously I did try to stay low-level and collect equipment,whitch
worked fine as a tourist.

Not this time.

I rambled through the dungeon and killed everything in sight.
Maybe that's overdoing it a little bit, I still had to be very carefull.
When I got a dagger as weapon I felt a little more safe.

My plan was to stick to daggers as weapons,get them to expert, and then
fling them when I got a stock. Then practice twoweaponing daggers,
later switch to longsword.

That would be in harmony with my most desirable artifacts as Neutral:
Magicbane, Vorpy or some of the Foo*brands. I'd like to go with Vorpy this
time because I never did that before.

Found +0 GoP in an armour-shop on level 2, that's luck.
Then an early altar on level 4, very good.

On level 5 I found the bones of Lung II + his dog Hachi.(I play on single-user
system and rarely get any bones). This gave me a +0 samurai sword and a cursed
sack, but nothing else of interest, apart from Hachi as my new pet.

I went on to do the Minetown/Soko/Minesend - combo,but Minetown had
just about nothing but candles and a crystal ball.
Soko on the other hand yielded an AoR, that's a plus.

Two levels before Minesend my brass-lantern goes hui. I decide to leave,
because I have two different kinds of gray stones anyway. Carry them both.

Some Foo dropped +0 Speed-Boots, wow. This is the second stroke of luck.

Later I stepped on polymorph-trap. Mastodon! 
Lost my nice +2 elven mithril and +1 Dwarf-cloak. No elven cloaks so far.
I had to play carefully and recover, AC was somewhat crappy now,
like 3 or 1 (don't remember this exactly).

Went to dig out vaults for protection and get 2 Points first.
Test some armor like dwarven mithril , down to -4 or so.

After some innocent sacrificing I receive my first gift Mjollnir.
Ok, enhance hammer to basic.I feel very condident now...

I move my stash to a cross-aligned temple on level 13, and (really, that was
an accident) did my water prayer in the temple of Offler. Ugh.
So I lost protection and had to face a Marillith of Offler.
What a drawback.

Surprisingly I found a Magic Lamp in a general-shop on 21.
Use it for light. 
Shop-wise this game was not so good: 2 general-, 2 armor- and one potion-shop in
the main-dungeon, and a hardware- and light-shop in the Mines.

Somewhere around this time an Aleax dropped a rustproof +2 Longsword. 
Perfect for twoweaponing!

I begin to slow down, damn Trices! Take a bite on dried reptiles.

I accidentally flung daggers on Priest of Offler in Stash-Tempel,when a
Werewolf appeared at the door. More spellbooks from the priest.
Already had been kitted out too well for him to succeed.
Now a murderer without telepathy,but cash.

Somehow I seem to recall that I had to kill two priests in this game,
but I'm not sure (been in the last few days, dammit).

Second gift is Magicbane: Great! Great! Finally Magic Resistance.
Mjollnir blows up wands (and rings?), I don't like that, but keep him as
a backup with me, and for Disenchanters.
That meant no boring sac-sessions in this game,which is cool.
Vorpy I would receive later when crowned.

Later I received Vorpy when crowned !

Found Ludious - an eel flung itself around me, when I got careless. 
Zapped it with WoTeleport.

Got silver scales from Ludious and made an SDSM. Ditch AoR for AoESP.

Accidentally stepped into Ludious-moat, diluted some scrolls.
Very tempted to smack myself for this faux-pas.

Crossed Ludious-moat with ?oEarth. Happily wasted all boulders to
prevent an accident at the entrance, very clever, isn't it ?

AGAIN stepped into Ludious-moat, burdened (with all that cash) :
lost Vorpy, magic Lamp, Luckstone, Magic Whistle, key, some wands,
and cleared various important potions/scrolls.

Here I have to say that not having a BoH is pain. Really.

Went back to stash and use my LAST ?oEarth to recover the items.
Now it's protection-time.

At Medusa a gray dragon did not leave scales, and I had no means of
levitation. No scrolls of Earth either. So what to do ?
Dig down and hope for Perseus' clothes or do Quest first? 
Hmmm.. that's an easy choice.

Quest! 
Got the PYEC,yay! and .. FINALLY found BoH on last Quest-level !!!

AND found a MagicMarker ! Last not least a ?oEarth and wand of cold.
The Tourist-quest turned out to be great, better than all other five 
quests I had previously seen.
Ready for the castle now.

Dig down at Medusa. Perseus has SoR and BoLevitation ,great.
I let Schroedinger's Cat play with a Poly-trap in Medusa's
living-room and get an Arch-Lich, ahhrg.

I go back and dump him in Sokoban. Too dangerous.

In the castle is another gray dragon - no scales.
But found another MM ! Apart from that 2 Lichs, a Ki-rin and a Titan.

Got the castle-wand and I decide to keep it for emergencies.
I have a scroll of genocide and another MM, and thus reverse-geno
gray dragons.

3 sets of scales !

Here I ask myself, why *did* I waste those ?oEA for my +4 SDSM ?
Hmmm.
Magicbane and the PYEC as only source of MR is .. risky (isn't it?).
I accept the mistake (or maybe I didn't plan on going wishless :)

VoTD piece of cake.

Shortly later, a gray dragon in Gehennom dropped scales, d'oh !
Well, ok, no harm has been done. But still.

I fling +5 daggers on Disenchanter. Stupid! Now got 3 +4 daggers.
Never did that before. Have to be more careful, this game seems like
an assembly of accidents to me. 

Never had any priest-accidents before, either.

You know you must not do that, then why *did* you do it then ?! 
Concentrate!

A Mindflayer on lvl 40 finally gave me back intrinsic telepathy.
No floating eye had left a corpse since the temple-accident.
Had the PYEC, anyway, but I like to take care for emergencies.

Damn shade stole me instrinsic speed. Zapped myself with WoSpeed.
Never found an WoEnlightenment.

Killed some Demon-Princes, found the Vib-Square and got the Candelabrum.

Yeenoghu showed up, accompanied by an Arch-Lich, but I didn't have
problems (pulse went up, of course).
Magicbane still worked great as primary weapon (twoweaponed
with a longsword), and Vorpy collected dust in my bag.

Why didn't I use one of my maybe five or six Silver Sabers ?
I lacked Scrolls of EW and decided to use my longsword,
because it's better on the planes.

I waited some 3.000 turns before the ascension-run to re-learn most
of my essential spells, whitch would then be expired. 
Planned it right this time. 
Just so annoying if you have to carry spellbooks with you to the
planes because they're just so damn heavy.

Then I went to Rodney's Tower and stepped onto a magic trap and had a 
(Master?)MindFlayer right next to me. This had happened several times 
in this game,but this time I got sucked once before I could engrave 
(it was my fault). Still four or five id-scrolls left, and lighted 
tunnels to the upstairs had been dug, so this was no problem.

Wasted an entire WoDeath on Rodney at his first re-appearance.
Because of the fabulous,incredible PYEC it didn't bother me at all.

Rodney also appeared in the Sanctum, double-troubled and went to play with
the high priest.
I watched the show for a while from outside, and when they lined up I got
them all three at once with a WoDeath. Bingo.

But Moloch complained a little about this and wasted no time sending down
some lighning-bolts.(Hmm, dont recall this from previous times,maybe the
priest was still peaceful because I didn't enter the sanctum?Just a guess.)

Unscared by Molochs ambitious greetings I grabbed the amulet, named it, 
and went back to the stairs.
That's right Moloch, there you have it.

The Mysterious force kicked in lots of times (ten? twenty?), but
eventually I surfaced back to the Dungeons of Doom.
Rodney was consequently greeted by a death-ray, and gave me no pain
this time.

The planes were uneventful, I used my crystal ball to detect the portal,
and went there. Period.
Teleported away some air-elementals. Luckily no Archons this time.

On astral I went first to right side. Famine. Sure that's not it, as 
expected - chaotic.

Somewhere I encountered a player-character with SDSM and whatnot,
whitch I just kept on missing all the time.
Took me easily more than 20 moves to dispatch the little bugger,
because he also had a !oFullHealing.

Then got hold on a Rubber Chicken and made some statues.

Next to the middle, where Death was lurking - lawful. Grumble,grumble.
So Pesty on the left side guarded my altar.

It just so *happens* to be the *last* altar for me, all the time!

Alright, there's no turning back now.
At the entrance a cockatrice appeared and left a corpse.
Didn't want to leave it lying around there,but I went burdened with it.
That's too risky for Pestillence,so I put it in my BoH.

Got deathly sick thrice, or so - it's always scary.
But I made it to the altar and sacced.


